# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use dry-run jobs to get the usage in resource units and service-side validation a job would incur on a real QPU without spending QPU time."
msgstr "Gunakan job dry-run untuk mendapatkan penggunaan dalam resource unit dan validasi sisi layanan yang akan dikenakan sebuah job pada QPU sungguhan, tanpa menghabiskan waktu QPU."

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs"
msgstr "Job dry-run"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run jobs {#dry-run-jobs}"
msgstr "Job dry-run {#dry-run-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job runs your workload through IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service without using any QPU time. Use a dry-run job to do the following before you commit to a real run:\n"
msgstr "Job dry-run menjalankan beban kerjamu lewat IBM Quantum&reg; Compute Service tanpa memakai waktu QPU sama sekali. Pakai job dry-run untuk melakukan hal-hal berikut sebelum kamu menjalankan yang sungguhan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the usage that the job would incur on the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**Mendapatkan penggunaan yang akan dikenakan job ini pada QPU sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Validate the job.** Quantum Compute checks the job's parameters, the same way it does for a real job.\n"
msgstr "**Memvalidasi job.** Quantum Compute memeriksa parameter job, sama seperti untuk job sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Get the [circuit timing schedule](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, if you request it, to debug the job before you run it for real.\n"
msgstr "**Mendapatkan [jadwal waktu circuit](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing)**, jika kamu memintanya, untuk men-debug job sebelum menjalankannya sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unlike dry-run jobs, local testing (fake backends and [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) runs on your own machine and therefore cannot provide usage numbers, service-side validation, or service timing information. To compare the two approaches, see [Mock devices compared to fake backends](#mock-vs-fake).\n"
msgstr "Berbeda dengan job dry-run, pengujian lokal (fake backend dan [Qiskit Aer](/guides/simulate-with-qiskit-aer)) berjalan di mesinmu sendiri sehingga tidak bisa memberikan angka penggunaan, validasi sisi layanan, atau informasi waktu dari layanan. Untuk membandingkan kedua pendekatan ini, lihat [Perangkat mock dibandingkan dengan fake backend](#mock-vs-fake).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 or later is required for dry-run jobs.\n"
"- Dry-run jobs are available in all regions, and are only available on the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans. They are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"- `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.51.0 atau yang lebih baru diperlukan untuk job dry-run.\n"
"- Job dry-run tersedia di semua wilayah, dan hanya tersedia di paket Flex, Premium, dan On-Prem. Job ini tidak tersedia di paket Open atau Pay-As-You-Go.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it works {#how-it-works}"
msgstr "Cara kerjanya {#how-it-works}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run a dry-run job, pass `dry_run=True` to the primitive's `run()` method:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan job dry-run, berikan `dry_run=True` ke metode `run()` milik primitive:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run` is an argument of the `run()` method (the default is `False`), not a runtime option. It is available to all primitives.\n"
msgstr "`dry_run` adalah argumen dari metode `run()` (defaultnya `False`), bukan opsi runtime. Argumen ini tersedia untuk semua primitive.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A dry-run job has the following characteristics:\n"
msgstr "Job dry-run punya karakteristik berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It runs in IBM Quantum Compute Service in the cloud, not on your machine.\n"
msgstr "Job ini berjalan di IBM Quantum Compute Service di cloud, bukan di mesinmu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "It uses the calibration data from the real QPU, not just a snapshot. \n"
msgstr "Job ini memakai data kalibrasi dari QPU sungguhan, bukan sekadar snapshot. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its results keep the expected schema and follow the expected shape of results from the real QPU, but contain randomized mock data. They are not actual or simulated measurement results, so do not use them to check physical correctness.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya mempertahankan skema yang diharapkan dan mengikuti bentuk hasil yang diharapkan dari QPU sungguhan, tetapi berisi data mock yang diacak. Hasil ini bukan hasil pengukuran asli atau hasil simulasi, jadi jangan dipakai untuk memeriksa kebenaran fisik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Processing happens on the server, so the job might not finish immediately.\n"
msgstr "Pemrosesan terjadi di server, jadi job mungkin tidak langsung selesai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit size, shots, and other limits are the same as for any job of that program.\n"
msgstr "Ukuran circuit, shot, dan batasan lainnya sama seperti untuk job apa pun dari program tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`dry_run=True` also works when the backend is already a mock device.\n"
msgstr "`dry_run=True` juga berfungsi ketika backend-nya sudah berupa perangkat mock.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the usage {#read-the-usage}"
msgstr "Membaca penggunaan {#read-the-usage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The usage of a completed dry-run job is the usage the same job would incur on the real QPU, except in rare situations where calibration data changes significantly after the dry-run job and before the job on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Penggunaan dari job dry-run yang sudah selesai sama dengan penggunaan yang akan dikenakan job yang sama pada QPU sungguhan, kecuali dalam situasi langka ketika data kalibrasi berubah signifikan setelah job dry-run dan sebelum job di QPU sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns the usage in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`job.usage()` mengembalikan penggunaan dalam detik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` returns the same data together with the usage status.\n"
msgstr "`job.metrics()[\"usage\"]` mengembalikan data yang sama beserta status penggunaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dry-run usage is not charged, does not consume your plan allocation, and does not count against any limits.\n"
msgstr "Penggunaan dry-run tidak ditagih, tidak memakai alokasi paketmu, dan tidak dihitung terhadap batasan apa pun.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Do not use job.usage_estimation with dry-run jobs\">\n"
"Do not use `job.usage_estimation` on a dry-run job. Use `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Jangan gunakan job.usage_estimation dengan job dry-run\">\n"
"Jangan gunakan `job.usage_estimation` pada job dry-run. Gunakan `job.usage()`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.usage()` returns `0` until the usage calculation is final, so wait for the job to finish before you read it.\n"
msgstr "`job.usage()` mengembalikan `0` sampai perhitungan penggunaan final, jadi tunggu job selesai sebelum membacanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Circuit timing schedule {#circuit-timing-schedule}"
msgstr "Jadwal waktu circuit {#circuit-timing-schedule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To request the circuit timing schedule, use the same option as for a real job. For full details, see [Visualize circuit timing](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"
msgstr "Untuk meminta jadwal waktu circuit, gunakan opsi yang sama seperti untuk job sungguhan. Untuk detail lengkap, lihat [Visualisasikan waktu circuit](/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitations {#limitations}"
msgstr "Keterbatasan {#limitations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Job and batch modes only.** Dry-run jobs can only run in [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) and [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"
msgstr "**Hanya mode job dan batch.** Job dry-run hanya bisa berjalan di [job mode](/guides/execution-modes#job-mode) dan [batch mode](/guides/execution-modes#batch-mode).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans only.** Dry-run jobs are not available on the Open or Pay-As-You-Go plans.\n"
msgstr "**Hanya paket Flex, Premium, dan On-Prem.** Job dry-run tidak tersedia di paket Open atau Pay-As-You-Go.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices {#mock-devices}"
msgstr "Perangkat mock {#mock-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices are the implementation behind dry-run jobs. Dry-run jobs hide mock devices by default, but you encounter them in these cases:\n"
msgstr "Perangkat mock adalah implementasi di balik job dry-run. Job dry-run menyembunyikan perangkat mock secara default, tetapi kamu akan menemukannya dalam kasus-kasus berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Instances configured to access only mock devices.** Example: if you use `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` to submit a dry-run job on `ibm_phoenix`, but your instance doesn't have access to `ibm_phoenix`,  you will get a `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Instead, select the mock device directly with `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"
msgstr "**Instance yang dikonfigurasi hanya untuk mengakses perangkat mock.** Contoh: jika kamu memakai `service.backend(\"ibm_phoenix\")` untuk mengirim job dry-run ke `ibm_phoenix`, tetapi instance-mu tidak punya akses ke `ibm_phoenix`, kamu akan mendapat `QiskitBackendNotFoundError`. Sebagai gantinya, pilih perangkat mock secara langsung dengan `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compute resources.** Mock devices are hidden by default on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page. The table on the page has a filter option to include them, but only the Flex, Premium, and On-Prem plans have access to mock devices.\n"
msgstr "**Compute resources.** Perangkat mock disembunyikan secara default di halaman [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). Tabel di halaman itu punya opsi filter untuk menyertakannya, tetapi hanya paket Flex, Premium, dan On-Prem yang punya akses ke perangkat mock.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Workloads table.** Jobs from mock devices are hidden by default on the [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page. The table has a filter option (the funnel icon) to display them.\n"
msgstr "**Tabel Workloads.** Job dari perangkat mock disembunyikan secara default di halaman [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads). Tabelnya punya opsi filter (ikon corong) untuk menampilkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Python API.** `service.backends()` and `service.jobs()` exclude mock devices unless you call them with `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock` indicates whether a backend is a mock device. `service.least_busy()` never returns a mock device.\n"
msgstr "**Python API.** `service.backends()` dan `service.jobs()` mengecualikan perangkat mock kecuali kamu memanggilnya dengan `include_mocks=True`. `IBMBackend.is_mock` menunjukkan apakah sebuah backend adalah perangkat mock. `service.least_busy()` tidak pernah mengembalikan perangkat mock.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mock-vs-fake\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mock devices compared to fake backends {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"
msgstr "Perangkat mock dibandingkan dengan fake backend {#mock-devices-compared-to-fake-backends}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The names are similar, but a mock device and a [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) are different things. A fake backend is a local object in your Python environment. A mock device is a cloud resource in IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
msgstr "Namanya mirip, tetapi perangkat mock dan [fake backend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider) adalah dua hal yang berbeda. Fake backend adalah objek lokal di lingkungan Python-mu. Perangkat mock adalah resource cloud di IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | Mock device (for example `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (for example `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| What it is | A device in IBM Quantum Compute Service | A Python class in `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Where it runs | Cloud, in the service | Locally, on your machine |\n"
"| How you get it | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, or automatically with `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Account and instance | Specific plans only (Flex, Premium, or On-Prem) | All instances and plans |\n"
"| Calibration | Live, matches the real device at any time | Fixed snapshot shipped with the installed package |\n"
"| Results | Randomized data with the expected schema. Not a simulation | Noisy simulation that uses the snapshot's noise model |\n"
"| Physically meaningful results | No. Never use them to check correctness | Approximately, within the limits of the noise model |\n"
"| Usage reported | Yes | None |\n"
"| Charged or counted against plan allocation or limits | No | No |\n"
"| Job validation | Done by the service, same as a real job | Limited to what the client checks |\n"
"| Timing schedule | Available on request  | Not available |\n"
"| Execution modes | Job and batch mode only. Sessions are blocked | Session syntax accepted but ignored (local mode has no real sessions or batches) |\n"
"| Completion | Asynchronous, on the server | Runs locally and returns when finished |\n"
"| Shown in platform interface and API lists | Hidden by default (Compute resources, Workloads table, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Opt in to show | Never, because nothing is sent to the service |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Perangkat mock (misalnya `mock_phoenix`) | Fake backend (misalnya `FakeManilaV2`) |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Apa itu | Sebuah perangkat di IBM Quantum Compute Service | Kelas Python di `qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider` |\n"
"| Tempat berjalan | Cloud, di dalam layanan | Secara lokal, di mesinmu |\n"
"| Cara mendapatkannya | `service.backend(\"mock_phoenix\")`, atau otomatis dengan `run(..., dry_run=True)` | `from qiskit_ibm_runtime.fake_provider import ...` |\n"
"| Akun dan instance | Hanya paket tertentu (Flex, Premium, atau On-Prem) | Semua instance dan paket |\n"
"| Kalibrasi | Langsung, sesuai dengan perangkat sungguhan setiap saat | Snapshot tetap yang disertakan dalam paket terinstal |\n"
"| Hasil | Data acak dengan skema yang diharapkan. Bukan simulasi | Simulasi ber-noise yang memakai model noise dari snapshot |\n"
"| Hasil bermakna secara fisik | Tidak. Jangan pernah dipakai untuk memeriksa kebenaran | Kurang lebih, dalam batas model noise |\n"
"| Penggunaan dilaporkan | Ya | Tidak ada |\n"
"| Ditagih atau dihitung terhadap alokasi atau batasan paket | Tidak | Tidak |\n"
"| Validasi job | Dilakukan oleh layanan, sama seperti job sungguhan | Terbatas pada apa yang diperiksa klien |\n"
"| Jadwal waktu | Tersedia berdasarkan permintaan  | Tidak tersedia |\n"
"| Mode eksekusi | Hanya mode job dan batch. Session diblokir | Sintaks session diterima tetapi diabaikan (mode lokal tidak punya session atau batch sungguhan) |\n"
"| Penyelesaian | Asinkron, di server | Berjalan secara lokal dan mengembalikan hasil saat selesai |\n"
"| Ditampilkan di antarmuka platform dan daftar API | Disembunyikan secara default (Compute resources, tabel Workloads, `backends()`, `jobs()`). Aktifkan untuk menampilkan | Tidak pernah, karena tidak ada yang dikirim ke layanan |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to choose {#how-to-choose}"
msgstr "Cara memilih {#how-to-choose}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **how much usage the job will consume, or whether the service will accept it**, use a dry-run job.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengetahui **berapa banyak penggunaan yang akan dihabiskan job, atau apakah layanan akan menerimanya**, gunakan job dry-run.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To find out **what the output might look like**, or to work offline, use a fake backend or Aer.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengetahui **seperti apa kira-kira outputnya**, atau untuk bekerja secara offline, gunakan fake backend atau Aer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "To do both, iterate on circuits and results with a fake backend, then dry-run as the last check before the real QPU.\n"
msgstr "Untuk keduanya, iterasikan circuit dan hasil dengan fake backend, lalu lakukan dry-run sebagai pemeriksaan terakhir sebelum QPU sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common points of confusion {#common-points-of-confusion}"
msgstr "Titik-titik yang sering membingungkan {#common-points-of-confusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A mock device is not a simulator.** Its output is random, so sampling a Bell circuit on `mock_phoenix` does not return a Bell distribution. If you want realistic noisy output, use a fake backend.\n"
msgstr "**Perangkat mock bukan simulator.** Outputnya acak, jadi men-sampling circuit Bell di `mock_phoenix` tidak mengembalikan distribusi Bell. Kalau kamu mau output ber-noise yang realistis, pakai fake backend.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A fake backend is not the live device.** Its calibration is a snapshot and might be out of date. A mock device tracks the real calibration, so transpiled circuits and timing match what the QPU sees today.\n"
msgstr "**Fake backend bukan perangkat yang live.** Kalibrasinya adalah snapshot dan mungkin sudah usang. Perangkat mock mengikuti kalibrasi sungguhan, jadi circuit yang di-transpile dan waktunya sesuai dengan apa yang dilihat QPU hari ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Neither runs on real hardware.** Neither consumes QPU time, but only a dry-run job goes through the service.\n"
msgstr "**Keduanya tidak berjalan di hardware sungguhan.** Keduanya tidak memakai waktu QPU, tetapi hanya job dry-run yang melewati layanan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`usage_estimation` is not the dry-run estimate.** For a dry-run job, `job.usage()` returns the seconds of usage your job would be charged on a real QPU.\n"
msgstr "**`usage_estimation` bukan estimasi dry-run.** Untuk job dry-run, `job.usage()` mengembalikan detik penggunaan yang akan ditagihkan untuk jobmu pada QPU sungguhan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use cases {#use-cases}"
msgstr "Kasus penggunaan {#use-cases}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Students and courses {#students-and-courses}"
msgstr "Pelajar dan kursus {#students-and-courses}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An administrator restricts an instance to mock devices only, using the QPU customization toggle when [creating or editing the instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Students then validate their payloads end-to-end without consuming real QPU time or RUs. Because the instance has access only to mock devices, students select the backend by its mock name:\n"
msgstr "Seorang administrator membatasi instance hanya untuk perangkat mock, memakai tombol kustomisasi QPU saat [membuat atau mengedit instance](/guides/instances#add-instance). Dengan begitu pelajar bisa memvalidasi payload mereka dari ujung ke ujung tanpa memakai waktu QPU atau RU sungguhan. Karena instance hanya punya akses ke perangkat mock, pelajar memilih backend lewat nama mock-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Project planning {#project-planning}"
msgstr "Perencanaan proyek {#project-planning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A team about to start a project dry-runs representative jobs to see the RUs the project needs, before choosing a plan or allocation:\n"
msgstr "Tim yang akan memulai proyek melakukan dry-run pada job yang representatif untuk melihat RU yang dibutuhkan proyek, sebelum memilih paket atau alokasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Final check before running on a real QPU {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"
msgstr "Pemeriksaan akhir sebelum berjalan di QPU sungguhan {#final-check-before-running-on-a-real-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate parameters and inspect the timing schedule with `dry_run=True`, then drop the argument and run on the real QPU. Nothing else in your code changes:\n"
msgstr "Validasi parameter dan periksa jadwal waktu dengan `dry_run=True`, lalu hapus argumen itu dan jalankan di QPU sungguhan. Tidak ada hal lain di kodemu yang berubah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah selanjutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
